## Communication Objectives

- Keep stakeholders informed
- Create clear decision-making channels
- Reduce confusion and delays
- Document risks, issues, changes, and approvals
- Establish a consistent reporting cadence

## Stakeholder Communication Matrix

| Audience | Information Needed | Format | Frequency | Owner |
|---|---|---|---|---|
| Executive Sponsor | Project status, risks, decisions | Executive summary | Biweekly | Project Lead |
| Client Project Team | Tasks, milestones, blockers | Status meeting | Weekly | Implementation Lead |
| Technical Team | Requirements, testing, defects | Working session | As needed | Technical Lead |
| Customer Success | Readiness, adoption, transition | Transition meeting | Before go-live | Implementation Lead |

## Meeting Cadence

| Meeting | Purpose | Attendees | Frequency |
|---|---|---|---|
| Internal Project Meeting | Review delivery progress | Internal team | Weekly |
| Client Status Meeting | Review milestones and risks | Client and project team | Weekly |
| Executive Update | Review decisions and major risks | Sponsors and leaders | Biweekly |
| Go-Live Readiness Review | Confirm launch approval | All key stakeholders | Before go-live |

